data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Keep a deque of indices. Its values never increase from front to back, so the front is the answer. For each new\nindex: drop the front index if it has left the window; drop the back indices whose values are not larger than the\nnew value; push the new index. Once the first window is complete, each step appends the front value. Each index is\npushed once and popped once, so the total work is O(n)."},"hints_note":null}

